# Mandatory UI libraries

Use only the libraries below for these concerns. Prefer existing project wrappers when present.

Do **not** introduce alternate libraries, native stand-ins, or ad-hoc reimplementations on your own. If the mandated stack is judged genuinely insufficient for the task, **stop, ask the user**, explain why an alternative is needed and what you propose, and **wait for explicit approval** before adding or using anything else.

## Forms & overlays: Radix UI

Use **Radix UI** (`radix-ui` / `@radix-ui/*`) for all general forms and overlays:

- Text, Select, Checkbox, Switch, Radio, Slider
- Dialog, Alert Dialog, Popover, Dropdown Menu, Context Menu, Tabs
- **Tooltip** (see below)
- Native `input` / `textarea` only when wrapped by Radix Form (or project ChatSelect / ConfirmModal patterns)

Do **not** use native `type="date"`, `type="datetime-local"`, or `type="time"` for new UI.

## Dates & times: React Aria Components

Use **`react-aria-components`** + **`@internationalized/date`** for date, date range, datetime, datetime range, and dedicated time pickers.

Prefer wrappers (`ChatDatePicker`, `ChatDateTimePicker`). Compose `DatePicker` / `DateRangePicker` / `DateField` / `TimeField` with `Calendar` / `RangeCalendar`. Wire values as `CalendarDate` / `CalendarDateTime` (and ranges); convert at API/storage boundaries if needed.

```jsx
// ❌ BAD
<input type="date" value={date} onChange={...} />

// ✅ GOOD
import { parseDate } from '@internationalized/date';
import { DatePicker } from 'react-aria-components';
```

## Color picker: react-colorful

Use **`react-colorful`** only (`HexAlphaColorPicker` / `HexColorPicker`, `HexColorInput`, etc.). Prefer **`HexAlphaColorPicker`** (+ `HexColorInput` with `alpha`) when the value may include transparency.

```text
❌ BAD — react-color, @uiw/react-color, native <input type="color">, custom canvas pickers
✅ GOOD — import { HexAlphaColorPicker, HexColorInput } from 'react-colorful'
```

## Animation: motion

Use the **`motion`** package only (`motion`, `motion/react`). Do not add `framer-motion` as a separate dependency or use other animation libs for UI motion.

```text
❌ BAD — framer-motion package, GSAP, anime.js, CSS-only hacks when a motion component/API is the fit
✅ GOOD — import { motion, AnimatePresence, animate } from 'motion/react' (or `motion`)
```

## Drag and drop: dnd-kit

Use **`@dnd-kit/core`**, **`@dnd-kit/sortable`**, and **`@dnd-kit/utilities`** only.

```text
❌ BAD — react-beautiful-dnd, @hello-pangea/dnd, react-dnd, native HTML5 DnD for app UI
✅ GOOD — DndContext, SortableContext, useSortable, CSS.Transform from @dnd-kit/*
```

## Tooltip: Radix only

Tooltips **must** use Radix (`Tooltip` from `radix-ui` or `@radix-ui/react-tooltip`). Do not use `title=`, custom hover divs, or other tooltip libraries as the product tooltip UI.

```jsx
// ❌ BAD
<button title="Save">...</button>

// ✅ GOOD
import { Tooltip } from 'radix-ui';
<Tooltip.Provider>
  <Tooltip.Root>...</Tooltip.Root>
</Tooltip.Provider>
```
